#: src/help/content.js:20
msgid "Library & system"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:28
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:30
msgid "Open any image from the Media Library via \"Edit Image\", or create a new document with File → New. Everything you do happens on layers, your original file is untouched until you save."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:34
msgid "\"Save to Media Library\" overwrites the attachment but keeps the previous file as a restorable version (History window, View → History, bottom section). \"Save as New Image\" creates a separate attachment. \"Export\" downloads a file without touching the library."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:38
msgid "Your work is protected: the editor autosaves in the background and offers to restore an unsaved session when you return."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:42
msgid "Documents open in tabs along the top: File → New, templates and Asset Library designs open next to your current work instead of replacing it. A dot on a tab marks unsaved changes; the + button starts another document."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:46
msgid "The editor tour starts only from Help → Show Tour. It follows your current Full or Easy Mode and never opens automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:50
msgid "Prefer a simpler surface? Help → Easy Mode swaps the editor chrome for a beginner shell with Start, Edit and Elements on the right and direct tools on the left; \"Switch to full editor\" brings everything back. The article Easy Mode has the details."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:54
msgid "Two doors reach everything without a menu: the magnifier in the title bar (⌘K) opens a search that finds every command, tool, filter, effect and extension by name, even with a typo, and Enter runs it. Help → Help Assistant opens a chat that answers \"how do I…?\" questions from this handbook and offers to play the matching tour."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:61
msgid "Create a new document"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:69
msgid "The tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:71
msgid "The eyedropper opens the Color panel and starts a loupe over the canvas at once: it samples a point or the average of a 3 by 3 or 5 by 5 square of document pixels, the loupe pauses while you are over the panel, and Alt at the start sends the color to the background instead. Pick on screen is the separate action for colors outside the canvas. The clone stamp needs a source first: Alt-click sets it. Its bar has size, opacity and hardness and an Aligned switch: on, the distance between source and brush stays across strokes, so a texture continues; off, every stroke starts again at the source. The effect brush blurs, sharpens, smudges, dodges, burns and sponges. With the pen, a click sets a corner, a drag pulls out handles and Alt breaks a handle pair; its freehand mode draws like a pencil and fits smooth anchors to the stroke on release, the fidelity decides how closely."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:75
msgid "Move (V) and Select (O) select and arrange layers. Marquee (M), Lasso (L) and Magic Wand (W) make selections; Smart Select (K) selects the object you click with local AI. Crop (C) trims the canvas."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:79
msgid "Brush (B), Pencil (N) and Eraser (E) paint and erase; the Paint Bucket (G) fills, Gradient (D) draws color ramps. The Clone Stamp (S) copies from an Alt-clicked source; the Blur/Sharpen brush (R) paints local focus changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:83
msgid "Text (T) and Shape (U) add vector layers, the Pen (P) draws paths. Eyedropper (I) picks colors, Hand (H) pans, Zoom (Z) magnifies. Hold Space anytime to pan."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:87
msgid "Each tool shows its options in the bar above the canvas, size, opacity, symmetry painting, shape type and more."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:97
msgid "Painting"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:99
msgid "The Brush paints into the layer you have selected, the way a brush should. Its panel opens with it and floats over the canvas, so every setting is in reach while you work: the tips down the left as real strokes rather than names, and everything else on the right."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:103
msgid "A style decides how the paint meets what is already there. Normal is plain blending. Watercolor, Gouache, Acrylic and Oil mix pigment instead, so blue over yellow turns green, and they carry what makes a medium recognizable: paint running out along a stroke, the dark rim of a drying wash, grain settling in the paper, thick paint catching the light. Smudge brings no paint of its own and pushes around what it crosses."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:107
msgid "Four dry media join them. Wax crayon and Colored pencil ride the tooth of the paper and leave its pores white until you press harder, and both glaze over paint that is already there: blue pencil over yellow reads green. The Airbrush keeps spraying while you hold still, in fine droplets at the fringe and an even film where it builds. Metal leaf lays small platelets of metal that mirror their surroundings, each at its own tilt, with a fine sparkle of pigment in them. Gold, Silver, Copper and Rose gold sit above the color wheel as a start."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:111
msgid "Color is a choice of three. Solid is the color you picked. Jitter gives every mark a shade of its own, which is what stops a stroke reading as printed by a machine. Gradient runs a ramp along the stroke, from where you set down to where you lift off."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:117
msgid "Press B for the Brush. Pick a tip from the strip on the left; every preview is a real stroke drawn by the engine that will paint it."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:121
msgid "Choose a style, then set size, hardness, opacity and flow."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:125
msgid "Pick a color on the wheel, and under it choose Solid, Jitter or Gradient."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:129
msgid "Paint. The stroke goes into the selected layer, or onto one of its own if you tick that at the foot of the panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:135
msgid "Every style comes with brushes tuned to it, pinned at the top of the tip strip. Picking a style puts the first of them in your hand."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:139
msgid "Without a pen, a stroke still starts and ends like one: it swells in, lifts off light, and a quick stroke lays less than a slow one. Taper, in the style's own section, sets how far; at 0 a mouse stroke lays full load end to end."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:143
msgid "With a pen, Pressure curve under Smoothing fits the pressure to your hand and tablet: 50 is the tablet as it comes, lower answers a light touch sooner, higher wants a firmer hand. A mouse has no pressure and ignores it."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:147
msgid "A wet brush carries a charge. It lays evenly until most of it is spent; then the water gives out first and the last of it breaks into dry brush, over the tooth and along the bristles. Going back over your own wet paint costs nothing, and lifting the brush reloads it. Paint load, in the style's own section, sets how far a charge goes; at 100 it never runs out."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:151
msgid "A selection works like masking film for every style: paint across its edge and only the inside takes the paint, with all of the medium's own behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:155
msgid "Draw a brush tip builds your own tip out of shapes, holes included. It is kept as a recipe, so it stays sharp at any size and travels inside the document."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:159
msgid "The Eraser takes the same tips. Erasing through a texture is a technique, not a curiosity."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:163
msgid "A right-click on the canvas brings the same settings up as a quick popover, for when you would rather not have the panel on screen."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:167
msgid "Symmetry in the options bar mirrors every stroke as you draw it, which is how you get a balanced ornament in one pass."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:176
msgid "Navigation & shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:178
msgid "Hold Space to pan, use ⌘/Ctrl +/− to zoom, ⌘0 fits the image, ⌘1 shows 100%. The Navigator (View menu) gives a minimap with a draggable viewport."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:182
msgid "Hold Alt with the Move tool to measure pixel distances to the canvas edges and other layers. Digit keys set the active layer’s opacity (5 = 50%). Right-click the canvas to pick between overlapping layers."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:186
msgid "View → Workspace shows and hides whole editor zones - or lets you click the parts you want gone - and sets the toolbar layout to one or two columns when the window is short. View → Guides & Grid adds grids, guide lines and snapping for precise layouts."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:190
msgid "Hold the Compare button (title bar) to see the saved original. Help → Keyboard Shortcuts lists every key."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:194
msgid "Every slider and number field in the editor is set the same way: Alt for fine steps, Shift for fast ones, a click on the readout to type an exact value. The article Sliders and number fields has the details."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:201
#: src/screens/editor-dialogs.jsx:124
msgid "Keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:205
#: src/screens/editor-menubar.jsx:1141
#: src/screens/workspace-dialog.jsx:81
#: src/screens/workspace-dialog.jsx:89
msgid "Workspace"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:209
#: src/lib/editor-themes.js:350
#: src/screens/editor-canvas.jsx:3525
#: src/screens/editor-menubar.jsx:1179
#: src/screens/guides-dialog.jsx:70
#: src/screens/guides-dialog.jsx:79
msgid "Guides & Grid"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:217
msgid "Sliders and number fields"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:219
msgid "Every value in a tool panel, a dialog or an extension is set the same way. Drag a slider for a quick change. Hold Alt while you drag for fine steps, so a value such as 90 percent is easy to hit even on a short slider. Hold Shift to move faster. A number field’s label is a handle too: pull it left or right to change the value without typing."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:223
msgid "Click a slider’s readout to type an exact value. Enter applies it, Tab or a click outside applies it too, and Escape restores the value from before you opened that editor. A decimal point and a decimal comma both work. Number fields that are already editable take typed values directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:227
msgid "Number fields carry compact arrows that match the light or dark theme. Click the upper arrow to add one step and the lower one to subtract; hold an arrow to keep going, and hold Shift for ten steps at a time. The keyboard works as well: the arrow keys change a focused slider by one step, Up and Down do the same in a number field, and Shift makes it ten. On a slider, Home and End jump to the limits and Page Up and Page Down move ten steps."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:231
msgid "The X, Y, width, height and font size fields have the same arrows and still take expressions such as 100+20, /2 or *1.5. Enter or leaving the field applies the expression, Escape discards the draft. Clicking an arrow while an expression is pending applies it once and then steps the result."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:235
msgid "Angle sliders with snapping pause at 45 degree intervals, 0°, 90° and 180° among them where the range allows. Alt-drag, keyboard steps and typed values pass those snap points, so 89° or 91° stay easy to reach."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:239
msgid "On/off settings are compact switches: click the switch or its label, or press Space when it has focus. Gray is off, the accent color is on. Square checkboxes remain for picking several files, formats or other items, and a dash in a group checkbox means only some of them are selected. Color fields join a swatch and an editable value: click the swatch for the color picker or type the value; a checkerboard means transparency."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:245
msgid "Press B for the Brush and set the size to 192. Hold Alt and drag a little to the right: 193. Drag back: 192."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:249
msgid "Open View → Navigator, click the zoom percentage and type 90. You enter the value in percent, even though the slider works on its own scale underneath."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:253
msgid "Select a layer, go to Properties → Transform and click the rotation readout. Type 90. Drag next to it and it snaps; hold Alt or use an arrow key and 89° or 91° is yours."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:259
msgid "A drag or a held arrow is one undo step when the setting changes the document. Tool options and dialog previews keep their usual history behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:263
msgid "Fields keep their limits and their increments. Decimal settings stay decimal, and a setting with fixed choices, such as the radius in Map Studio, picks the nearest supported choice."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:267
msgid "Many sliders jump back to their default on a double-click. That is the slider’s own feature, not the number editor’s, so not every field has it."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:276
msgid "Color panel and eyedropper"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:278
msgid "Color is a main panel on the right, with solid colors, gradients, patterns, presets and color tools. Solid-color swatches open a small picker at the top right; gradient and pattern swatches open the full editor. An already visible full editor is reused. Both views start with the color wheel. Open gradients & patterns in the small picker opens the full editor with the same target."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:282
msgid "Color follows the selected object and shows its actual fill. Fill and Stroke switch the paint target. While editing text, choose selected characters or the entire text. A swatch for a shadow or a gradient stop edits that specific color. The eyedropper icon and I open Color and start the canvas pixel loupe immediately. The loupe pauses over panels; Esc ends sampling."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:286
msgid "With one shape or text layer selected, the tool rail shows a Fill and a Stroke swatch that open the panel on that target. A stroke can carry a gradient too, and a stroke that was 0 px wide gets 2 px as soon as it gets a color. The Gradient tool opens the same panel in its gradient view: without a gradient layer selected you edit the settings for the next gradient, after drawing one the panel follows that layer, and New gradient prepares the next."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:290
msgid "The Edit tab starts with the Solid, Gradient and Pattern cards. Solid shows the color wheel by default, with color field, RGB, HSL and grayscale views, HEX and an opacity bar from transparent to the full color. Gradient shows the visual editor: presets in a column on the left with search and your own gradients, then the preview, the stops with Add, Remove and Reverse, the type and angle, and Gradient settings for spreading, spread, midpoint and geometry. Pattern shows the pattern previews and your own patterns, with scale and Manage patterns. Explore colors folds in the harmonies as rows of tiles, a lock and Tune, Compare colors with Original, A and B, and the background preview; Sampling holds the sample size and Pick on screen."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:294
msgid "The Swatches tab lists standard, grayscale, document, favorite, recent, image, saved and Brand Kit palettes. Hovering a swatch previews it on the target, a click applies it. Collect picks up to twelve colors from the canvas into a set you can save as a palette. The Apply, Find and Gradient switch decides what a click does: Find marks and selects every layer that uses the color, Gradient turns two to eight swatches into a linear, radial or angle fill, previews it, applies it in one undo step or saves it as a gradient preset. Sample line drags a line over the picture and returns eight colors along it. Paste palette reads HEX, RGB, HSL or CSS text and keeps the colors as an imported palette."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:298
msgid "Tools holds the tools for whole designs. Linked colors let a stroke or text color follow another color with a lightness offset and keep following when the source changes. Palette mix maps the document’s colors onto a second palette with a slider from 0 to 100 percent and applies the result in one step. Result color computes the color a half-transparent shape needs so that a chosen point on the canvas ends up exactly in the color you want."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:304
msgid "Select a shape and click the eyedropper icon. The panel opens on Fill and the loupe is live; click a color in the picture and the shape takes it."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:308
msgid "Switch to Swatches, choose Gradient, click three swatches, pick Radial and press Apply. The fill of the selected text or shape becomes that gradient."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:312
msgid "Choose Find, click a swatch and press Select: every layer in that color is selected and its groups unfold in the Layers panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:318
msgid "Favorite in the footer stars the current color; Palettes opens the Color Schemer with what the panel shows, the harmony or the palette under Swatches."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:322
msgid "The full Color panel stays open when switching tools. Colors in dialogs stay local until Apply; Cancel discards them. Named palettes require WordPress; favorites and collected colors also work in standalone mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:331
msgid "Themes panel"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:333
msgid "View → Tool Panels → Themes opens a card panel that gathers the tools, panels, dialogs and studios for one kind of work. Pick a theme at the top: Art & Painting, Vector & Shapes, Photo & Retouch, Text & Typography, Patterns & Backgrounds, Layout & Branding, 3D & Scenes, Motion & Video, Maps & Posters, Print & Craft, Data & Diagrams or Content & Automation. A theme named like a category of the Extensions menu shows exactly the studios of that category. The cards come in small groups, and the last theme you chose comes back the next time."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:337
msgid "A tool card activates the tool and opens its settings beside the panel. A panel card switches the right-hand panel to Layers, Properties, Adjust, Effects or AI Studio, and shows that tab even when your workspace hides it. A studio card opens the full studio; when it closes, the theme is still there. Only installed studios appear, so a theme never shows a card that leads nowhere, and an empty theme points to the extensions manager."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:341
msgid "The panel starts beside the toolbar, 280 by 600 pixels, and works like every other tool panel: pin it to keep it open while you switch tools, collapse it, drag it, resize it. Switching a theme changes nothing in the document, the tool or the workspace, and loads no studio in advance."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:347
msgid "Text on a card inserts a text layer in the middle of the canvas, ready to type, and the panel stays open. Mask needs a layer that already has a mask."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:356
#: src/screens/easy/easy-bar.jsx:47
#: src/screens/easy/easy-panel.jsx:121
#: src/screens/easy/easy-panel.jsx:125
#: src/screens/editor-menubar.jsx:1568
#: src/screens/onboarding-steps.js:56
msgid "Easy Mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:358
msgid "Help → Easy Mode swaps the editor chrome for a simpler shell; the choice is remembered for this site, and Switch to full editor brings everything back at any time. Documents, layers, dynamic bindings, saving and undo are the same as in the full editor, so nothing is lost on the way there or back."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:362
msgid "The right side has three areas. Start offers cards for Text, Shapes, Improve photo and Draw, and the recommended creative functions with an arrow to the full Creative & AI choice. Edit shows the settings of the selected element or of the active drawing or crop tool in the sub-tabs Basics, Looks and Layout: text content, font, size, bold, italic, color and alignment; fill, stroke color, width and position for shapes, with a pencil icon that opens the full shape dialog; brightness, contrast, saturation and Remove background for images; opacity right in each section. Elements is the layer list with previews, groups, reordering, locking and deleting."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:366
msgid "The left bar has ten direct entries: Select, Creative, Text, Shapes, Draw, Eraser, Crop, Photo, Looks and Layout. Creative opens the themed choice of studios and dialogs, Shapes opens the Shape Studio, Draw shows Brush, Pencil and Eraser with color and the basic sliders, Crop brings the crop panel with its format cards. The Asset Library tray at the bottom stays the one library for templates, photos, icons and text lockups. A fixed design row at the foot of the panel holds the document background, the pixel size and Resize with format groups."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:372
msgid "Help in Easy Mode is a small menu with Handbook and Show Tour; the tour follows Easy Mode and never starts on its own. Floating tool panels and the small context bar stay out of Easy Mode, their pins and positions are kept for the full editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:381
#: src/screens/editor-canvas.jsx:3838
#: src/screens/editor-menubar.jsx:1083
#: src/screens/editor-menubar.jsx:3029
#: src/screens/editor-menubar.jsx:3034
#: src/screens/panels/color-panel.jsx:2331
#: src/screens/panels/gradient-editor.jsx:545
#: src/store/constants.js:542
#: src/store/ops/repeat-ops.js:60
#: src/store/ops/repeat-ops.js:97
#: src/store/ops/repeat-ops.js:171
#: tools/brush-lab/stage/lab.js:3784
msgid "Repeat"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:383
msgid "Repeat (J) gives any layer or group a live Repeat layer that lays out copies for you: in a row, a grid, a circle or along a path you draw in the panel. Click a layer with the tool and the copies appear at once, wrapped with the source in a Repeat group. Change the source, and every copy follows; change the rule, and the layout follows."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:387
msgid "The panel holds the rule: the mode on the left, then copies, step or gap, columns and rows, radius and sweep, or the path with its presets (line, arc, wave, S-curve) and whether copies stay upright or turn with the path. Stack decides whether the copies sit behind or in front of the source. A few handles on the canvas set the same values by dragging: the step of a row, the ring of a circle, the frame of a path."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:391
msgid "Progression changes the copies over their run: size, opacity, rotation and color each get an end value and a curve, so a headline can trail ninety-nine copies one pixel apart that shrink and fade to black, and still follow every edit of the text. Bake turns the copies into real layers inside the group and switches to Move; Remove dissolves the Repeat and keeps the source."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:397
msgid "Press J, click a text layer. The row of copies appears with the panel; set Copies to 99, Step X and Step Y to 1."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:401
msgid "Under Progression turn on Opacity with an end value of 0 and Color with black as the end color. The long shadow is done, and it follows the text when you retype it."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:405
msgid "Switch the mode to Circle and drag the ring handle on the canvas to set the radius; Sweep decides whether the copies close the circle or stop on an arc."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:411
msgid "The Repeat layer in the Layers panel carries the repeat icon; select it to get the panel and the handles back. Selecting the source alone gives you the source’s own tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:415
msgid "Grid Repeat and Radial Repeat from the Edit menu are folded into this tool."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:424
msgid "Layers, groups & masks"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:426
msgid "The Layers panel lists everything in your document, top to bottom. Drag to reorder, double-click a name to rename, right-click for actions and color labels. The filter box finds layers by name."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:430
msgid "Each layer has opacity and a blend mode (how it mixes with layers below). Groups organize layers; a clipping mask restricts a layer to the shape of the one beneath it. Right-click offers Copy Styles / Paste Styles to transfer opacity, blend mode, filters and effects onto other layers, even in another tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:434
msgid "The right-click menu on the canvas is grouped: Edit, Convert, Combine, Arrange, Group & Mask and Layer. The Arrange row moves a layer to the front or back (Shift+Cmd+] and [), one step (Cmd+] and [), flips it or turns it a quarter; the Layer group renames, hides (Shift+Cmd+H), locks (Cmd+2) and deletes. Cmd+G groups, Shift+Cmd+G ungroups, Shift+Cmd+V pastes a copy exactly where it was copied from, and Select > Select Same picks every layer with the same fill, stroke, font or type. Where layers overlap, the menu lists everything under the cursor. Alt-click an eye in the Layers panel to see that layer alone, and the folder button beside the filter collapses every group."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:438
msgid "A layer mask hides parts of a layer without deleting them: add one via Layer → Add Layer Mask, then paint on the mask with black (hide) or white (show). Click the mask thumbnail to target it."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:442
msgid "Smart Objects preserve their content: filters applied to them stay editable as Smart Filters, and \"Edit Contents\" opens the embedded document."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:446
msgid "Edit → Replace Colors swaps one color for another across the whole page: fills, strokes, text, styled characters, gradient stops, effects and the background, with a before/after preview and one undo step. Each hit keeps its own transparency."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:450
msgid "With several layers of one kind selected, Properties shows Mixed where fills, stroke colors or widths differ. Typing a value sets it for every editable layer in the selection in one undo step; locked layers and the children of locked groups stay as they are."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:459
msgid "Selections"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:461
msgid "The marquee draws rectangles or ellipses, the lasso works freehand or as a polygon (click the corners, double-click or Enter closes), and both bars carry the modes New, Add and Subtract plus a feather, so a touch screen has what Shift and Alt give a keyboard. Select > Modify expands, contracts, smooths or borders any selection by a number of pixels."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:465
msgid "Selections limit painting, filling and many commands to a region. Marquee drags rectangles, Lasso draws freeform shapes, the Magic Wand selects by color, set its tolerance in the options bar, or disable \"Contiguous\" to select a color across the whole image."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:469
msgid "Select → Smart Select finds the main subject automatically (local AI, no key needed); the Smart Select tool (K) does the same for the object you click. Shift adds to a selection, Alt subtracts."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:473
msgid "Refine with Select → Feather (soft edges), save selections for later, or invert them. Remove Object fills the selection with reconstructed background."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:482
msgid "Resizing: image, canvas & design"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:484
msgid "Image → Image Size scales the whole document - every layer with it - to new pixel dimensions. Image → Canvas Size changes only the working area: layers keep their size, space is added or removed around them."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:488
msgid "Image → Resize Design rescales a whole layout to a new format in one step: layers scale and reposition to fit the target size - ideal to turn a wide banner into a square post or a story."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:494
msgid "For photos: Image → Image Size, enter the new dimensions, confirm."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:498
msgid "For more room to design: Image → Canvas Size and enlarge the working area."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:502
msgid "For a new format of a finished layout: Image → Resize Design and pick the target size."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:509
#: src/screens/editor-menubar.jsx:393
#: src/screens/resize-dialog.jsx:157
#: src/screens/resize-dialog.jsx:169
