#: src/screens/vignette-dialog.jsx:1050
#: src/store/constants.js:499
#: tools/brush-lab/stage/lab.js:3741
msgid "Text"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:528
msgid "The Text button in the toolbar drops a ready-to-type box in the middle of the canvas. Press T instead to place text yourself: click to start typing at that spot, or drag first for a fixed-size box the text wraps in. Escape cancels, clicking outside commits."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:532
msgid "With the Text tool armed (T), clicking near a drawn line binds the text to the curve (Text on Path; right-click it later and choose \"Edit Path\" to bend the curve), and clicking inside a shape flows the text inside its outline (Text in Shape). Both also live in the right-click menu of a path or shape."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:536
msgid "Fluid Text (the switch in the context bar, in the options bar beside the curve, or in the Character section) lets the box set the type: every line fills the width of the frame and the words spread over as many lines as the height allows, so the text re-flows while you drag. Layouts put a look on top, from stacked poster capitals to an editorial lockup; the look re-flows with the box and your text stays editable. Switching Fluid Text off freezes the current look into the layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:540
msgid "Number fields in the Properties panel take arithmetic: \"100+20\", \"/2\" or \"*1.5\" work on the current value, and the chain between W and H keeps the proportion while you type. With several layers selected, a fill, stroke, font or size change hits all of them."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:544
msgid "The Character section (Properties panel) controls font, size, weight, spacing and color. The font picker previews the families that are ready to use, all served from your own site; the rest of the catalog can be downloaded under Settings, Fonts."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:548
msgid "Settings → Fonts adds more sources: upload your own woff2, woff, ttf or otf files (house fonts), or enable the optional Google Fonts CDN catalog. Both appear as extra groups in the font picker."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:552
msgid "Bold, italic, underline and strikethrough sit in the options bar and the Character section; a selection inside the text takes them as character styles. Case sets uppercase, lowercase or capitalized words without changing the stored text, and Paragraph spacing adds air between paragraphs without empty lines."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:556
msgid "For thumbnail-style text add an outline, a hard shadow or a pill background; the Curve slider bends text along an arc."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:560
msgid "The Effects tab holds one-click Text Styles (Gold, Chrome, Sticker, Comic, Neon sign, Glitch, Slime and more) plus single effects you can stack: shadows, glows, outlines, bevel, image fill, marker highlights, glitch, drips, confetti, pixelate, motion blur and a set of warp shapes. Everything stays editable text."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:564
msgid "The Text panel, the floating panel of the Text tool, lists the active effects of the layer at the top: a click on a name opens its controls, the x removes just that effect with one undo step. Layer effects such as shadows and glows have their own Blending tab there, with the parameters right under each switch; the outline stays under Appearance."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:574
msgid "Filters & effects"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:576
msgid "The Adjust panel combines one-click preset filters (thumbnails), Auto corrections, pixel effects and manual sliders (brightness, contrast, saturation, temperature and more)."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:580
msgid "Effects like Gaussian Blur, Vignette, Halftone or Glitch permanently change pixel layers, but applied to a Smart Object they become Smart Filters, which you can re-edit, reorder or disable anytime in the Properties panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:584
msgid "Image → Colors → Load LUT applies professional .cube color-grading files. Levels and Curves offer precise tonal control; Auto Levels/Contrast/Color fix common problems in one click."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:588
msgid "In Adjust → Fine tune, hold Compare to see the layer without its slider adjustments; release, Esc or a click elsewhere brings them back. It compares the sliders only, not filters or effects, and it is not the saved original from the title bar."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:594
msgid "Tools → Vignette & Film opens a small studio for vignettes and film grain: the result is an editable overlay layer that adapts when the design is resized."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:598
msgid "With a photo selected, Vignette & Film can put the overlay on that photo only, as a clipping mask, so text and logos above it stay untouched."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:606
#: src/lib/core-generators.js:27
#: src/lib/editor-themes.js:356
#: src/screens/editor-menubar.jsx:1484
#: src/screens/vignette-dialog.jsx:437
#: src/screens/vignette-dialog.jsx:498
#: src/screens/vignette-dialog.jsx:507
msgid "Vignette & Film"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:614
msgid "Design tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:616
msgid "The Tools menu bundles small design studios. Color Schemer suggests matching palettes and recolors your document in one click; Background Studio generates backgrounds in your colors, from soft light and gradients to shapes and patterns."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:620
msgid "The Color Schemer shows a palette on your own design, in several variants side by side, and Apply to design recolors it in one undo step: every editable color becomes a palette color, dark to dark and light to light, and photos stay as they are. Palettes come from the harmony cards and the wheel, from an image or the document. Saved palettes can be renamed, duplicated, sorted and deleted with Undo; As gradient hands the palette to the Color panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:624
msgid "Background Studio offers mesh gradients, organic and geometric shapes, low-poly, topographic lines, halftone, rings, confetti, terrazzo, plaid and scales, a starfield, and soft light: gradients, glow, aurora and bokeh. Looks start from a finished picture with a palette of its own; colors come from the document, your Brand Kits, saved palettes or chance, and the styles that tile also save as seamless patterns."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:628
msgid "Screenshot Beautifier frames a screenshot in a card, a browser or app window, a phone, a tablet or a glass rim, lays it out centered, rising from the bottom edge or running into a corner, tilts it on request and puts a backdrop behind it: a gradient or pattern, a blurred copy of the shot or a solid color."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:632
msgid "The Mockup Generator puts your design onto a studio-style product shot: phone, tablet, monitor, book, box, documents, framed print or canvas print, with camera angles, light, material presets and an optional reflection in the floor. Chart & Table turns data (pasting from Excel/Sheets works) into chart or table layers that stay editable."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:636
msgid "View → Check Contrast audits your text layers against WCAG contrast rules and shows which combinations are hard to read."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:640
msgid "Everything a tool inserts is a normal layer, so you can keep editing with the full toolset afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:644
msgid "A framed screenshot and a mockup open again from the right-click menu: Edit Screenshot Beautifier replaces the frame and its backdrop in place, and Edit Mockup keeps the background color a mockup can sit on."
msgstr ""

#: src/help/content.js:651
#: src/lib/editor-themes.js:387
#: src/screens/color-schemer-dialog.jsx:629
#: src/screens/color-schemer-dialog.jsx:709
